From 05b382425c1ab3496f28fb7416a817b0b5a0fe8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manrique <125496885+hashd1ve@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:30:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] dsv41: a marked request's prompt pass writes extra taps
 of the streams to a file

TF_DS_XTAPS=L,L,... and TF_DS_XTAPS_DIR on rank 0 (unset: no buffer, no launch). A request with "taps": "name"
has its prompt pass write, for each listed layer, the mean of the streams entering it for every row the pass runs
there, to DIR/name.xtaps (xtaps.zig has the format). The taps read the streams without changing them: a pending MoE
post goes to a scratch copy. Such a pass starts at the prompt's first token (no kept state) and runs every layer on
every row (replay 0) unless the name ends in .replay; its chunks absorb their last window rows into the drafter,
which is what a served chunk already does.
